## reading
- after_off is within the round-to-round spread of base: the kill switch removes the cost on this path.
- spans+metrics (no log write) and the written records each add a measurable cost on this ~3 ms in-process path; it is NOT negligible relative to this path and is reported as measured. In-process ASGI with no network/LLM/storage makes the relative share maximal; real requests with LLM/storage I/O were not measured.
- memory: maxrss differs by < 1 MB between variants (ring buffer bounded at 512 records). Log volume ~2.0 KB per chat request (~6.5 records).
- limits: shared sandbox CPU, single client, sequential, one route; no production load applied; no criterion is declared passed.
- correction to the line above: records/request = 6.00 (computed in the summary: 13800 lines / 2300 requests), not ~6.5.
